From: Armada:EVO <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: add PCIe1 suspend OPP

The AYANEO Pocket family enables PCIe1 for its Renesas uPD720201 USB
host. Give that controller the same 1000 kBps suspend-only DDR/LLCC
floor as PCIe0. Without an opp-suspend entry, the common Qualcomm PCIe
s2idle path drops PCIe1's OPP to NULL; after cluster collapse the AOP
can fail to return control.

The synthetic frequency and omitted opp-level keep this OPP out of
active link-speed matching. The upstream D3cold and generic PCI power
control paths still power down the link, PHY, endpoint, and modeled
Renesas supplies; this entry retains only the SM8550 wake contract.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
@@ -2642,6 +2642,19 @@
 					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_nom>;
 					opp-peak-kBps = <3938000 1>;
 					opp-level = <4>;
+				};
+
+				/*
+				 * Suspend-only DDR/LLCC floor for Pocket-family boards
+				 * that enable PCIe1 for the discrete Renesas USB host.
+				 * The synthetic frequency and absent opp-level prevent
+				 * active-link selection.
+				 */
+				opp-suspend-1 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_min_svs>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <1000 1>;
+					opp-suspend;
 				};
 			};
 
